    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "BeLettings are delighted to present No. 16 Brookford Park, Rush, Co. Dublin to the market. This attractive two-storey semi-detached home is ideally positioned within a quiet cul-de-sac setting and offers well-proportioned accommodation, an enclosed rear garden and excellent access to the many amenities Rush has to offer.\n\nThe property is presented in turnkey condition throughout, having recently undergone a number of upgrades including renovated bathrooms, new flooring and fresh internal paint, making it an ideal choice for those looking for a home that requires little or no work.\n\nUpon entering, the welcoming hallway provides access to the kitchen/dining room, measuring approximately 3.61m x 3.78m, with ample room for dining.\nTo the rear is the main living accommodation and guest WC. The generously sized living room, measuring approximately 4.59m x 5.27m, is a bright and comfortable reception space and offers an excellent area for both relaxing and entertaining and direct access towards the rear garden. \n\nUpstairs, the property offers three bedrooms, providing excellent flexibility for families, first-time buyers or those requiring a home office. The principal bedroom measures approximately 3.63m x 3.11m and benefits from an ensuite. Bedroom Two measures approximately 3.54m x 2.85m, while Bedroom Three measures approximately 2.62m x 2.23m. A recently renovated family bathroom completes the first-floor accommodation.\nExternally, the property benefits from communal off-street parking to the front, while a side entrance leads through to the enclosed rear garden, providing a private outdoor space with excellent potential for outdoor dining, entertaining or family use.\n\nBrookford Park is ideally located within the popular coastal town of Rush, offering a wonderful balance between village living, coastal amenities and commuter connectivity. Rush town centre is within easy reach and provides a selection of shops, cafés, restaurants, pubs and local services, while the area also benefits from a strong range of sporting and community facilities. \n\nThe location is particularly appealing for families, with Rush National School approximately 430m away and St. Joseph's Secondary School approximately 1.1km away alongside a number of other primary and secondary schools in the surrounding area. \n\nRush is renowned for its beautiful coastline, with both North Beach and South Beach nearby. South Beach stretches for approximately 2.4km and is backed by established dunes, while North Beach offers a sandy coastal setting and harbour. \n\nFor commuters, Rush & Lusk railway station provides regular commuter services towards Dublin and beyond, while local bus services also provide connections towards Dublin City Centre and surrounding areas. The M1 and Dublin Airport are also readily accessible by road."
      },
